            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for to print and publish, then the Tamil for to compile."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: புதிர்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "புதிர் — putir — \"a puzzle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தாத்தா ஒவ்வொரு நாளும் நாளிதழில் வரும் புதிருக்கு விடை கண்டுபிடிக்கிறார். tāttā ovvoru nāḷum nāḷitaḻil varum putirukku viṭai kaṇṭupiṭikkiṟār. Every day grandfather solves the puzzle in the newspaper."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "To set someone a puzzle is புதிர் போடு (putir pōṭu); to solve one is to find its answer: புதிருக்கு விடை கண்டுபிடி."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "புதிர் (putir) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4163 gives பிதிர் and புதிர் (putir), \"a riddle, a puzzle\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
